      },
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i001xr:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Document somewhere. But where? What docs did you bother to read when you started? If I had documented it somewhere, would you have found it? Where would you have looked? I’ll add it there?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe in the “Docutmenation” folder – a ‘debugging tricks’ – or ‘usage tricks and hints’?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "As for vector[3] – You maybe on the right track, but a KEY difference is that String is a class and c_str() is a method.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "vector (or Sequence perhaps you meant) is a TEMPLATED class, and [] are overloaded operators. However, I just noticed – the following DOES work:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "s.operator[](0)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "(at least on windoze).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe I should document that in the same place?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "As for GCC – I don’t remember. If I writeup docs for the above – I’ll writeup equiv for gcc. I’m 99% sure the answer is yes (there is an evaluation window). But somewhat this depends on the gui fornt-end to gdb you use.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
